  Privapp permission whitelist for com.qualcomm.location (IZat location service).

  WHY THIS FILE EXISTS:
  com.qualcomm.location is a privileged app (system/priv-app) that requests
  signature|privileged permissions. Android 9 enforces the privapp permission
  whitelist (ro.control_privapp_permissions=enforce), and when a privileged app
  requests a permission that is not whitelisted, PermissionManagerService
  throws during systemReady():

      java.lang.IllegalStateException: Signature|privileged permissions not in
      privapp-permissions whitelist:
      {com.qualcomm.location: android.permission.CONTROL_LOCATION_UPDATES}

  That exception crashes system_server on every boot, so Android's Rescue Party
  fires after 3 attempts and reboots to recovery.

  The permissions below are the signature|privileged ones the APK actually
  requests (verified with `aapt dump permissions`).
-->
<permissions>
    <privapp-permissions package="com.qualcomm.location">
        <permission name="android.permission.CONTROL_LOCATION_UPDATES"/>
        <permission name="android.permission.PROCESS_OUTGOING_CALLS"/>
        <permission name="android.permission.READ_PHONE_STATE"/>
    </privapp-permissions>
</permissions>
